10 REM D-DBLNORM: is a near-cancelling double difference normalised? (value, compare, exponent byte)
20 DEFDBL A-Z
30 A=5.0000000000001#:B=5:X=A-B:GOSUB 100
40 A=4.0000000000001#:X=A-4:GOSUB 100
50 X=1.0000000000001#-1:GOSUB 100
60 X=-5.0000000000001#+5:GOSUB 100
70 R=0:R=R+ABS(5.0000000000001#-5):X=R:GOSUB 100
80 X=1.2345678901234#-1.2345678901233#:GOSUB 100
85 X=123.45678901234#-123.45678901233#:GOSUB 100
90 X=1E-13:GOSUB 100:END
100 V=VARPTR(X):LPRINT X;-(X<1E-8);-(X>0);PEEK(V);PEEK(V+1);PEEK(V+2):RETURN
